 "text": "Hello, how are things with you? You need a cool box with a cold pack. If the box is big enough, leave it outside your kitchen overnight. Use ice cubes if you can get them. They last a lot longer than ice. A thick winter jacket helps too. Keep the lid off the cooler during the day, so it doesn't get cold inside. And a thin water bag inside the ice helps it last longer. He needs to learn the rhythm of cold ice to hot food. Show him how it feels with his hand. Yes, completely. Pour it into clean bottles and leave them overnight outside on a cold night. They' be drinkable by tomorrow.",
